## 2. Security Audit

### 🚨 CRITICAL — Hardcoded API Key in Test File

`tests/honest_audit.py` line 3: [raw.githubusercontent](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ncsound919/VibeServe/main/tests/honest_audit.py)
```python
os.environ["DEEPSEEK_API_KEY"] = "sk-d11b338d040441deaefdb552b80275ab"
```
A **real DeepSeek API key** is committed in plaintext in the public repo. The CI pipeline even runs TruffleHog to catch exactly this, but it uses `base: HEAD~1` (only scans the last commit diff), so it missed this key in an older commit. **This key should be rotated immediately.** [raw.githubusercontent](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ncsound919/VibeServe/main/.github/workflows/ci.yml)

### 🔴 HIGH — Python Auth Fail-Open

`verify_token()` in `auth.py` — when `VIBESERVE_API_SECRET` is not set: [raw.githubusercontent](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ncsound919/VibeServe/main/vibeserve/auth.py)
```python
log.warning("VIBESERVE_API_SECRET not set — authentication DISABLED (allow-all)")
return {"sub": "anonymous", "scope": "mcp:read mcp:write"}
```
This is fail-open. A missing secret silently grants all tool access to any caller. The `create_token()` function correctly raises `RuntimeError` if no secret is set — `verify_token` should do the same.

### 🔴 HIGH — Hardcoded Fallback JWT Secret (IDE)

`hono.ts` — in non-production environments, falls back to: [raw.githubusercontent](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ncsound919/VibeServe/main/ide/src/server/hono.ts)
```
'super-secret-jwt-token-with-at-least-32-characters-long'
```
While it throws in production if not set, the default is a known public string. Any token signed with this secret would validate in dev/staging. Should use `crypto.randomBytes` to generate a per-process secret if none is provided.

### 🟡 MEDIUM — `AUTH_BYPASS` Flag [raw.githubusercontent](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ncsound919/VibeServe/main/ide/src/server/hono.ts)

```typescript
const AUTH_BYPASS = process.env.NEXUS_AUTH_BYPASS === 'true' && process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development';
```
The CI pipeline sets `NEXUS_AUTH_BYPASS: true` for E2E tests. If `NODE_ENV` is ever accidentally left as `development` on a deployed instance, the entire auth layer is bypassed. [raw.githubusercontent](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ncsound919/VibeServe/main/.github/workflows/ci.yml)

### 🟡 MEDIUM — In-Process Rate Limiter (Both Layers)

**Python** `TokenBucket` (middleware.py) — explicitly documented as `in-process, no Redis`. Each worker process maintains its own token bucket state. A user can triple their effective rate limit by hitting 3 Uvicorn workers. [raw.githubusercontent](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ncsound919/VibeServe/main/vibeserve/middleware.py)

**Node.js** `rateLimiter` (hono.ts) — has a comment: `"For production multi-instance: configure with external store (e.g. Redis via @hono-rate-limiter/redis)."` Not implemented. [raw.githubusercontent](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ncsound919/VibeServe/main/ide/src/server/hono.ts)

### 🟡 MEDIUM — `_evict_stale()` Threshold Bug

In `TokenBucket.allow()`: [raw.githubusercontent](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ncsound919/VibeServe/main/vibeserve/middleware.py)
```python
if len(self._tokens) > 1000:
    self._evict_stale()
```
Eviction is only triggered after **1,000 unique identities** accumulate. Under slow drip traffic from hundreds of IP addresses, the dict grows unbounded until 1,001 is hit. Should instead call eviction on a time-based interval (e.g., every 5 minutes via a background task).

### 🟢 Strengths
- `hmac.compare_digest()` used for constant-time signature comparison — correct [raw.githubusercontent](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ncsound919/VibeServe/main/vibeserve/auth.py)
- JWT expiry (`exp` claim) correctly enforced
- Supabase JWT verifies `aud: 'authenticated'` claim — audience is checked [raw.githubusercontent](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ncsound919/VibeServe/main/ide/src/server/hono.ts)
- Browser command allowlist blocks arbitrary CLI injection [raw.githubusercontent](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ncsound919/VibeServe/main/ide/src/server/hono.ts)
- `_resolve_workspace_path()` in pipeline_tools correctly enforces workspace chroot [raw.githubusercontent](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ncsound919/VibeServe/main/vibeserve/tools/pipeline_tools.py)
- `sanitize_for_display()` strips HTML/ANSI/null bytes before audit log output
- Audit logs record all auth failures, RBAC denials, rate limit violations, and codegen events

